## New Work Order form rules (on-screen)

1. First choose **Equipment** or **Area**.
2. Equipment: `engineering/maintenance.php?type=getEquipmentForBreakdownByDepartment`; fallback `getEquipmentByDepartment`.
3. Area: `getAreasByDepartment` / location / section; manual name if empty.
4. Do **not** show Equipment/Area ID # on the screen form.
5. **Sub-Component ID#** auto-filled readonly.
6. Use `wof` theme — not a paper/scanned document layout.

## PDF format (FEN-001-01-A Issuance Log) — agents must keep

When editing `downloadIssuanceLogPdf` (Engineering **Issuance Log (Final)** print):

1. **Landscape A4** (paper is landscape)  
2. Medicap logo top-left (`phpmedicap/logos/medicap-logo.png`); `Ref: WI-EN-001-01` top-right  
3. Control header: TITLE **WORK ORDER ISSUANCE LOG FORM** | FORM NO. **FEN-001-01-A** | DEPT/QA APPROVAL (SIGNATURE/DATE) | REV **00** | EFFECTIVE **MAY 06 2025** | PAGE **1 OF 1**  
4. Data columns exactly: Work Order # | Date of Initiation | Initiated By & Date | Brief Description of Problem | Closed By & Date  
5. Pad blank rows like paper; confidential footer right-aligned  
6. Draw with TCPDF cells (not a loose HTML mock) so print matches paper  

**Engineering Issuance Log screen:** shows WOs after department verification (`status=ISSUANCE` → `CLOSED` + `TO_QA`), all departments. **Download Issuance Log** = Form A PDF above.

**Department Work Order Log:** that dept only; Form A/B downloads as documented.

## PDF format (FEN-001-01-B) — agents must keep

When editing `downloadWorkOrderPdf` only:

1. Logo (Medicap Laboratories) top-left  
2. Ref: WI-EN-001-01 top-right  
3. Control header: TITLE / FORM NO. FEN-001-01-B / DEPT & QA APPROVAL / REV 00 / EFFECTIVE DATE / PAGE  
4. Work Order #  
5. **Part A-The Initiator:** with Name, ID #, Sub-Component ID#, Is this, availability, problem, NCR, Submitted By/Date  
6. Footer: Submit to Engineering… completion of Part A  

## Status flow

```text
Equipment:
  TO_ENGG_REVIEW → TO_PART_B → TO_VERIFY → (TO_QA?) → CLOSED

Area:
  TO_ENGG_REVIEW → TO_PART_B (Work Performed + Interior/Exterior checklist dropdown) → TO_VERIFY → (TO_QA?) → CLOSED
```

After initiating-dept **Verification**: record appears on Engineering **Issuance Log** (CLOSED immediately, or TO_QA until QA closes).

**Area on Work Performed:** choose **Interior (FEN-001-01-C)** or **Exterior (FEN-001-01-D)** from dropdown, fill checklist + work performed, then save.

**Issuance Log:** **View** shows full WO (initiator → review → checklist → work performed → verify → QA).

## Department scoping

- Dept log / new / verification: initiating dept only  
- Engineering Review / Work Performed: `scope=all`  
- Issuance Log: `scope=all&status=ISSUANCE` (CLOSED + TO_QA) + PDF FEN-001-01-A  
- Never hardcode department names  

## UI theme

- `src/app/equipment-work-order/work-order-form.theme.css` (`wof__*`)  
- Header `--app-primary`, Close red, actions blue/green  
- Sidebar Work Order icon blue like Calibration — never orange  

## Developer do / don’t

1. Never restyle on-screen WO forms to match paper; paper = PDF only.  
2. Never duplicate module per department.  
3. Never use “Part A/B/C” in screen/hub titles (PDF body may use Part A label).  
4. Deploy PHP + `logos/medicap-logo.png` when changing PDF layout.  
5. Same pattern as `/preventiveimain`.
